1
00:00:01,612 --> 00:00:05,358
(Q11) Welcome to the Fiddy Working Heritage Farm.

2
00:00:05,358 --> 00:00:14,940
This open-air museum gives you the experience of agriculture and rural life in the English countryside at the end of the nineteenth century.

3
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:23,153
So you'll see a typical farm of that period, and like me, all the staff are dressed in clothes of that time.

4
00:00:23,153 --> 00:00:28,334
I must give you some advice and safety tips before we go any further.

5
00:00:28,334 --> 00:00:33,800
[Q11答案句] As it's a working farm, please don't frighten or injure the animals.

6
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:39,435
(Q12) We have a lot here, and many of them are breeds that are now quite rare.

7
00:00:39,435 --> 00:00:43,172
And do stay at a safe distance from the tools:

8
00:00:43,172 --> 00:00:49,477
[Q12答案句] some of them have sharp points which can be pretty dangerous, so please don't touch them.

9
00:00:49,477 --> 00:00:52,296
We don't want any accidents, do we?

10
00:00:52,296 --> 00:01:01,509
(Q13) [Q13答案句] The ground is very uneven, and you might slip if you're wearing sandals so I'm glad to see you're all wearing shoes

11
00:01:01,509 --> 00:01:05,019
we always advise people to do that.

12
00:01:05,019 --> 00:01:08,424
(Q14) Now, children of all ages are very welcome here,

13
00:01:08,424 --> 00:01:17,328
and usually even very young children love the ducks and lambs, so do bring them along next time you come.

14
00:01:17,328 --> 00:01:22,362
[Q14答案句] I don't think any of you have brought dogs with you, but in case you have,

15
00:01:22,362 --> 00:01:27,712
I'm afraid they'll have to stay in the car park, unless they're guide dogs.

16
00:01:27,712 --> 00:01:37,911
I'm sure you'll understand that they could cause a lot of problems on a farm.

17
00:01:37,911 --> 00:01:42,223
(Q15（地图题）) Now let me give you some idea of the layout of the farm.

18
00:01:42,223 --> 00:01:48,192
The building where you bought your tickets is the New Barn, immediately to your right,

19
00:01:48,192 --> 00:01:55,821
and we're now at the beginning of the main path to the farmland - and of course the car park is on your left.

20
00:01:55,821 --> 00:02:01,648
The scarecrow you can see in the car park in the corner beside the main path,

21
00:02:01,648 --> 00:02:10,226
is a traditional figure for keeping the birds away from crops, but our scarecrow is a permanent sculpture.

22
00:02:10,226 --> 00:02:16,193
It's taller than a human being, so you can see it from quite a distance.

23
00:02:16,193 --> 00:02:19,840
(Q16) If you look ahead of you, you'll see a maze.

24
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:27,520
It's opposite the New Barn, beside the side path that branches off to the right just over there.

25
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:34,192
The maze is made out of hedges which are too tall for young children to see over them,

26
00:02:34,192 --> 00:02:38,628
but it's quite small, so you can't get lost in it!

27
00:02:38,628 --> 00:02:44,297
(Q17) Now, can you see the bridge crossing the fish pool further up the main path?

28
00:02:44,297 --> 00:02:51,304
If you want to go to the cafe, go towards the bridge and turn right just before it.

29
00:02:51,304 --> 00:02:57,074
Walk along the side path and the cafe's on the first bend you come to.

30
00:02:57,074 --> 00:03:04,640
The building was originally the schoolhouse, and it's well over a hundred years old.

31
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:13,913
As you may know, we run skills workshops here, where you can learn traditional crafts like woodwork and basket-making.

32
00:03:13,913 --> 00:03:21,506
(Q18) You can see examples of the work, and talk to someone about the courses, in the Black Barn.

33
00:03:21,506 --> 00:03:26,762
If you take the side path to the right, here, just by the New Barn,

34
00:03:26,762 --> 00:03:32,184
you'll come to the Black Barn just where the path first bends.

35
00:03:32,184 --> 00:03:39,642
(Q19) Now I mustn't forget to tell you about picnicking, as I can see some of you have brought your lunch with you.

36
00:03:39,642 --> 00:03:45,144
You can picnic in the field, though do clear up behind you, of course.

37
00:03:45,144 --> 00:03:52,808
Or if you'd prefer a covered picnic area, there's one near the farmyard: just after you cross the bridge,

38
00:03:52,808 --> 00:03:56,349
there's a covered picnic spot on the right.

39
00:03:56,349 --> 00:04:01,107
(Q20) And the last thing to mention is Fiddy House itself.

40
00:04:01,107 --> 00:04:08,592
From here you can cross the bridge then walk along the footpath through the field to the left of the farmyard.

41
00:04:08,592 --> 00:04:13,418
That goes to the house, and it'll give you a lovely view of it.

42
00:04:13,418 --> 00:04:21,186
It's certainly worth a few photographs, but as it's a private home, I'm afraid you can't go inside.

43
00:04:21,186 --> 00:04:23,686
Right. Well, if you're all ready, we'll set off on our tour of the farm.

